## 🐛 Bugs I Hit & Fixed (Real Examples From My Projects)

| Mistake | Fix | Why |
|---|---|---|
| `CMD ["java","Main]` | `CMD ["java", "Main"]` | `CMD` needs a valid JSON array — every string quoted, brackets closed |
| `npm build` | `npm run build` | Custom npm scripts must be invoked with `npm run <script>` |
| `docker build -t portfolio-app.` | `docker build -t portfolio-app .` | Missing space merges the tag and build context into one argument |
| `docker run -p 8000:8000` (app on port 3000) | `docker run -p 3000:3000` | Host:container port mapping must match the port the app actually listens on inside the container — `EXPOSE` alone doesn't fix a wrong `-p` |

---

## 💡 Quick Tips
- `docker ps -a` first when something "isn't working" — check if the container even started.
- `docker logs <container>` before anything else when debugging a crash.
- Order Dockerfile instructions from **least to most frequently changing** to maximize layer caching (e.g., install dependencies before copying source code).
- `EXPOSE` is documentation only — it does **not** publish the port. Use `-p` to actually map it.
